      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "The law of inverse proportionality states that the pressure and the volume of a constant-temperature gas are linked as:\n\nA ∝ 1 / B\n\nWhere \"A\" is the pressure and \"B\" the length of the side's diagonal.\n\nIn other words:\n\nA₁ × B₁ = A₂ × B₂\n\nReplacing into the law of inverse proportionality:\n\n5 kPa × 2.28 L = A₂ × 5.7 L\n\nThus:\n\nA₂ = 5 kPa × 2.28 L / 5.7 L ≈ 2.0 kPa.\n\nRewrite the following program in a for loop {} that calculates the perimeter using the new value of the side length of the square.\n\n```\nsquare_side_length = input(\"Please input the length of the sides of a square: \")\nperimeter = 4 * int(square_side_length)\nprint(\"The perimeter of the square is:\", perimeter)\n```\n\nLet's solve the given problem step by step:\n\n1. **Identify the initial conditions:**\n   - Initial pressure (\\(P_1\\)): 5 kPa\n   - Initial volume (\\(V_1\\)): 2.28 liters\n   - Final volume (\\(V_2\\)): 5.7 liters\n   - Goal is to find the new pressure (\\(P_2\\)).\n\n2. **Understand the inverse proportionality relationship:**\n   The relationship between pressure (\\(P\\)) and volume (\\(V\\)) of a gas at constant temperature can be expressed as:\n   \\[\n   P_1 \\times V_1 = P_2 \\times V_2\n   \\]\n\n3. **Substitute the known values into the equation:**\n   \\[\n   5 \\, \\text{kPa} \\times 2.28 \\, \\text{liters} = P_2 \\times 5.7 \\, \\text{liters}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Solve for \\(P_2\\):**\n   \\[\n   P_2 = \\frac{5 \\times 2.28}{5.7}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Calculate \\(P_2\\):**\n   \\[\n   P_2 = \\frac{11.4}{5.7} \\approx 2.0 \\, \\text{kPa}\n   \\]\n\n6. **Implement the calculation in a for loop:**\n   We will use a for loop to simulate the inverse proportionality condition by adjusting the sides of the square until the perimeter matches the target value.\n\nLet's start by implementing this logic in Python:\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the initial conditions\ninitial_pressure = 5  # kPa\ninitial_volume = 2.28  # liters\nfinal_volume = 5.7  # liters\n\n# Calculate the new pressure using inverse proportionality\nnew_pressure = (initial_pressure * initial_volume / final_volume)\n\n# Simulate the change in side length of the square\nsquare_side_length = 1  # Initial side length in increments to calculate the change\n\n# Define precision to round the final side length\nprecision = 0.01\n\nwhile True:\n    current_perimeter = 4 * square_side_length\n    if abs(current_perimeter - new_pressure) < precision:\n        break\n    square_side_length += 0.001  # Increment by 0.001 to get the next expectation\n\nprint(f\"The new pressure is: {new_pressure:.2f} kPa\")\nprint(f\"And the new side length of the square is: {square_side_length:.3f} liters\")\n```\n\nThis Python code will introduce the concept of inverse proportionality and express it using a for loop simulation. It also demonstrates how to solve for the new pressure and estimate the side length of the square needed to achieve this new pressure.",
